{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgEN3TW6CnhsXG1wodrGS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The system prompt is now split into two cached blocks, but this probably doesn't stop the full re-cache on most messages yet. The static block likely falls under the model's minimum cacheable size, explained below. I checked the split offline only and made no API calls, so I haven't measured the effect on real usage numbers.\n\n**The change** (`build_system` in `bot.py`): the system prompt used to be one block with one cache marker. A cache hit requires the start of the prompt to match exactly, so each `save_fact` changed that block and forced a full re-cache. That's the pattern in `logs/usage.jsonl`: after every save, `cache_read` drops to 0 and `cache_creation` is about 1,050. Now there are two blocks, each with its own cache marker:\n1. **`INSTRUCTIONS`**: the coaching rules, with no date, name or other values inserted.\n2. **`athlete_context(...)`**: the date, profile, zones, goal, facts and language.\n\nOffline, block 1 came out identical across both athletes, across dates, and before and after a fact was added. Tool filtering is unchanged, and I updated the caching paragraph in `README.md`. `ANSWER.md` has the details and the steps to verify.\n\n**The catch:** `claude-sonnet-4-5` caches only prompt prefixes of at least 1,024 tokens and silently ignores markers on shorter ones. From the logs, the tools plus the instructions (everything before the athlete block) come to roughly 900–930 tokens on messages that send only the two core tools:\n- **Messages that pull in the plan or race tools:** that part is about 1,100+ tokens, so a memory write re-caches only the ~130-token athlete block.\n- **Messages with only the core tools (most of them):** the first marker is probably ignored, so a memory write still re-caches all ~1,050 tokens.\n\nTwo ways to get it over 1,024; I haven't done either:\n- **Always send `plan_week` and `predict_race`:** about 150–250 extra tokens per call, but read from cache at about 10% of the price, and the tool list would never change. `NOTES.md` says to keep keyword filtering, so I left that decision to you.\n- **Add more fixed coaching content to `INSTRUCTIONS`.**\n\nAlso, Opus 4.5 and Haiku 4.5 need at least 4,096 tokens, so switching `MODEL` to either would turn off caching for both blocks.\n\n**To check:** run the bot, tell it a fact, then send another message. In `logs/usage.jsonl`, `cache_read` should be about 900 and `cache_creation` about 130. If `cache_creation` is still about 1,050, you're hitting the 1,024-token minimum."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1424,"cache_read_input_tokens":35465,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1424},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"afe0c820-3ab2-49d8-a92b-1b9a44f960f8","uuid":"44d78ba8-6e68-4a41-ad25-7c6bd3eb3b48","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:33:42.063Z","request_id":"req_011CgEN3SpfEbgJzCBV1Tc1S"}
